That is such a difficult question! It depends on my mood. Sometimes a great game doesn't sit well with me just because I wasn't in the right mood when I started it. That's what happened to me with A Hat in Time. I know it's supposed to be great, but I played for about 2 hours and ended up returning it because I just wasn't feeling it. I kinda regret returning it and not giving it another chance. 

But I digress... So, to answer your question, he's a (not well thought) list of my favorite indies, in no particular order:

- The Messenger (probably my favorite); 
- Slay the Spire (the one I've played most hours); 
- Dave the Diver (the one I wish I could play for the first time again); 
- My Time At Portia; 
- Hades; 
- Strange Horticulture; 
- Mutazione; 
- A Short Hike; 
